---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout title="AI Visibility Fix Pack — Product Schema, robots.txt and llms.txt, $49 | GeoScore"
  description="Done-for-you GEO fixes for one product: Product JSON-LD completed and validated (variant offers, price, currency, availability, identifiers), a robots.txt diagnosis naming the AI crawlers your rules block and the exact lines to delete, a hand-written llms.txt, and a re-audit after you deploy. $49 one-time, 48-hour delivery."
  schema={{
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'FAQPage',
    mainEntity: [
      {
        '@type': 'Question',
        name: 'What does the Fix Pack include?',
        acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: 'Product JSON-LD for one best-seller, completed and validated: every variant offer with price, currency and availability, plus the sku, gtin or mpn identifiers a shopping surface uses to match your product elsewhere. Plus a robots.txt diagnosis: which AI crawlers your rules block on that page and the exact lines to delete — I do not rewrite your file. Plus a curated llms.txt written by hand from what your site publishes publicly (not a platform template), a 1-page audit summary, and a re-audit with before/after scores once you have deployed the files.' }
      },
      {
        '@type': 'Question',
        name: 'How is this different from the free fix file generator?',
        acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: 'The free generator produces a generic skeleton from your homepage title and description. The Fix Pack is built by a human from your public pages, checked against your live robots.txt and schema, and verified with a re-audit after deployment. You are paying for the catalog work, the checking, and the verification — not for three files any chatbot can draft.' }
      },
      {
        '@type': 'Question',
        name: 'Does llms.txt actually get read by AI engines?',
        acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: 'Rarely, on current evidence. Ahrefs\' June 2026 study of 137,210 domains found 97% of published llms.txt files got zero requests in May 2026, and Google says it ignores the file. We include a hand-written llms.txt because it is free, harmless, and read by some agents and tools — but the measurable parts of this pack are the robots.txt diagnosis and the Product schema. We will never promise you citations.' }
      },
      {
        '@type': 'Question',
        name: 'Do you guarantee rankings or AI citations?',
        acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: 'No — and no honest provider can. AI answers depend on the engines, your content, and your market. What we guarantee is the deliverable: correct, catalog-specific files, deployed-ready, plus a re-audit showing exactly what changed in your 11-dimension score.' }
      },
      {
        '@type': 'Question',
        name: 'How do I order and pay?',
        acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: 'Email us your store URL at hello@geoscore.help first and get a free 1-paragraph diagnosis. If the diagnosis shows real gaps and you want to proceed, we complete and deliver the fix files within 48 hours, followed by a post-deployment re-audit.' }
      },
      {
        '@type': 'Question',
        name: 'What do you need from me?',
        acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: 'Just your store URL and which product sells best. No admin access, no passwords. On Shopify, llms.txt is not a file you upload — since May 2026 the platform generates /agents.md and points /llms.txt at it, and the only supported override is a theme template (Online Store > Themes > Edit code > Templates > add llms.txt.liquid). We write that template for you and your developer adds it in one step. Two things we handle so you do not break anything: a custom template replaces Shopify\'s output instead of merging with it, so it must carry the UCP and MCP discovery links across, and it renders in a restricted Liquid context where shop, collections and pages are blank — so the content is curated and static rather than generated from your catalogue, and it needs a refresh when your range changes. Plain-HTML and WordPress sites get files they can drop in as-is.' }
      }
    ]
  }}>
  <section class="max-w-4xl mx-auto py-12">
    <div class="text-center mb-10">
      <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-3 py-1.5 rounded-full text-xs font-medium bg-brand-500/10 text-brand-400 border border-brand-500/20 mb-4">
        Done for you · One-time payment
      </div>
      <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl font-extrabold mb-4 tracking-tight">
        AI Visibility <span class="gradient-text">Fix Pack</span>
      </h1>
      <p class="text-lg text-gray-400 max-w-2xl mx-auto">
        Your product data, made machine-readable. We check what a shopping agent can actually parse,
        fix what is missing, and re-audit after you deploy.
        <span class="text-white font-semibold">$49 one-time · 48-hour delivery.</span>
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- The problem, with receipts -->
    <div class="card p-6 md:p-8 mb-8">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold mb-4">Why most stores are invisible to AI search</h2>
      <div class="text-sm text-gray-400 space-y-3">
        <p>
          On 2026-11-01 we parsed the product page of 25 well-known direct-to-consumer stores for
          <span class="font-mono text-gray-300">Product</span> structured data. 16 served a product node, and
          <strong class="text-gray-200">13 of those carried every property a shopping surface needs</strong> —
          name, image, and an offer with price, currency and availability. The other three were each missing one.
          That split is the honest picture, and it decides what you actually need: on Shopify the platform already
          emits most of this, so the work is finding the variant offers, identifiers and offer blocks that are
          wrong or empty. On WooCommerce, Webflow or a custom build the usual number is zero.
        </p>
        <p>
          When a shopper asks ChatGPT or Perplexity for a product, the engine can only use what its crawlers
          can read. On 2026-11-01 we checked the <span class="font-mono text-gray-300">llms.txt</span> and <span class="font-mono text-gray-300">robots.txt</span>
          of 25 well-known direct-to-consumer stores ourselves. <strong class="text-gray-200">20 of them return an
          <span class="font-mono text-gray-300">llms.txt</span>, and not one describes what the store sells.</strong>
          17 serve the platform's agent-integration guide — it explains how an agent should build a cart and
          where the MCP endpoint lives, and says nothing about the catalogue. 3 serve a skeleton with no
          product facts. 2 return 404, and the rest are rate-limited or broken.
        </p>
        <p>
          Access is not the problem. 23 of those stores publish a readable
          <span class="font-mono text-gray-300">robots.txt</span>, 4 mention GPTBot or ClaudeBot, and exactly one
          blocks anything at all. The problem is that the file an AI reads when it arrives says nothing about
          the business. On general websites the gap looks different again: across our separate audit of 324
          sites the median scores <strong class="text-gray-200">41/100</strong> and
          <strong class="text-gray-200">75.9%</strong> have no <span class="font-mono text-gray-300">llms.txt</span>
          at all, because no platform generates one for them.
        </p>
        <p>
          Run the <a href="/" class="text-brand-400 hover:underline">free GeoScore audit</a> on your store first.
          If your structured data, crawler access or AI guidance dimensions are weak, this pack fixes exactly those files.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Deliverables -->
    <div class="card p-6 md:p-8 mb-8">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold mb-4">What you get</h2>
      <ul class="text-sm text-gray-300 space-y-3">
        <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-brand-500">✓</span><span><strong class="text-white">Product JSON-LD, completed and validated</strong> — for your best-seller: every variant's offer with price, currency and availability, plus the identifiers (sku, gtin, mpn) a shopping surface uses to match your product to the same product elsewhere. Validated before delivery, and we tell you exactly which properties were missing when we started.</span></li>
        <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-brand-500">✓</span><span><strong class="text-white">robots.txt diagnosis</strong> — which AI crawlers your current rules block on that page, and the exact lines to delete so they can get in. <strong class="text-white">I do not rewrite your file</strong>: appending an <code class="text-gray-200">Allow:</code> never overrides a longer <code class="text-gray-200">Disallow:</code>, so a merged "patch" would silently do nothing — and re-allowing a bot you deliberately blocked is your call, not mine.</span></li>
        <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-brand-500">✓</span><span><strong class="text-white">A curated llms.txt</strong> — written by hand from what your site publishes publicly: categories, best-sellers, the pages worth reading. On Shopify this ships as a theme template that keeps your UCP and MCP discovery links intact. Included because it is free and harmless, not because we can promise it gets read — see the FAQ below.</span></li>
        <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-brand-500">✓</span><span><strong class="text-white">1-page audit summary</strong> — your 11-dimension scores and the exact gaps the files address, in plain language.</span></li>
        <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-brand-500">✓</span><span><strong class="text-white">Post-deploy re-audit</strong> — once the template or files are live, we re-run the audit and send before/after scores. If the override did not take effect, you see it here, not months later.</span></li>
      </ul>
      <p class="text-xs text-gray-500 mt-4">
        Need more products or sitewide schema? The extended pack ($129) covers up to 10 products — simply ask via email.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Honest note on llms.txt -->
    <div class="card p-6 md:p-8 mb-8">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold mb-4">An honest note on llms.txt</h2>
      <div class="text-sm text-gray-400 space-y-3">
        <p>
          The largest log study so far — Ahrefs, June 2026, server logs from 137,210 domains — found that
          <strong class="text-gray-200">97% of published llms.txt files received zero requests in May 2026</strong>,
          and no major AI provider has said it reads the file. Google's AI search guide says it is not
          required and is ignored by Google Search. So we do not sell llms.txt as a citation lever — and you
          should be suspicious of anyone who does.
        </p>
        <p>
          Why include one at all? It costs nothing, does no harm, and some AI agents and developer tools do
          fetch it — and if anything reads yours, a file that actually describes what you sell beats the
          platform's protocol guide. The parts of this pack with machine-verifiable effect are the Product
          schema and the robots.txt diagnosis, and the post-deploy re-audit shows you exactly what changed.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- How it works -->
    <div class="card p-6 md:p-8 mb-8">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold mb-4">How it works</h2>
      <ol class="text-sm text-gray-300 space-y-3 list-none">
        <li class="flex gap-3"><span class="font-bold text-brand-400">1.</span><span><strong class="text-white">Free diagnosis first.</strong> Email your store URL to <a href="mailto:hello@geoscore.help?subject=Fix%20Pack%20Consultation%20%26%20Diagnosis%20%E2%80%94%20My%20Store%20URL" class="text-brand-400 hover:underline">hello@geoscore.help</a>. You get a 1-paragraph diagnosis of what AI crawlers actually see — free, no obligation.</span></li>
        <li class="flex gap-3"><span class="font-bold text-brand-400">2.</span><span><strong class="text-white">Confirm & $49 delivery.</strong> If the diagnosis shows real gaps and you decide to proceed, confirm via email. No admin access or passwords are ever requested.</span></li>
        <li class="flex gap-3"><span class="font-bold text-brand-400">3.</span><span><strong class="text-white">Delivery within 48 hours.</strong> A Shopify theme template (<span class="font-mono text-gray-300">llms.txt.liquid</span>) that keeps your UCP/MCP discovery links intact, or drop-in files for plain HTML — with install notes for both.</span></li>
        <li class="flex gap-3"><span class="font-bold text-brand-400">4.</span><span><strong class="text-white">You deploy, we re-audit.</strong> Paste the files (or hand them to your developer), tell us via email that they're live, and receive your before/after re-audit report.</span></li>
      </ol>
      <div class="mt-6">
        <a id="fixpack-email-cta" href="mailto:hello@geoscore.help?subject=Fix%20Pack%20Consultation%20%26%20Diagnosis%20%E2%80%94%20My%20Store%20URL" class="block w-full text-center px-6 py-3.5 rounded-xl font-semibold text-white bg-gradient-to-r from-geo-600 to-brand-600 hover:from-geo-500 hover:to-brand-500 shadow-md shadow-brand-500/20 hover:shadow-brand-500/30 transition text-base">
          Email store URL for free diagnosis (hello@geoscore.help) →
        </a>
      </div>
      <p class="text-xs text-gray-500 mt-3 text-center">Built and delivered by Deng Li, developer of GeoScore — the same engine that scores this site 94/100.</p>
    </div>

    <!-- FAQ (must stay in sync with the FAQPage schema above) -->
    <div class="max-w-2xl mx-auto">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-center mb-6">Fix Pack FAQ</h2>
      <div class="space-y-4">
        <div class="card p-5">
          <h3 class="font-semibold mb-2">What does the Fix Pack include?</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-gray-400">Product JSON-LD for one best-seller, completed and validated: every variant offer with price, currency and availability, plus the sku, gtin or mpn identifiers a shopping surface uses to match your product elsewhere. Plus a robots.txt diagnosis: which AI crawlers your rules block on that page and the exact lines to delete — I do not rewrite your file. Plus a curated llms.txt written by hand from what your site publishes publicly (not a platform template), a 1-page audit summary, and a re-audit with before/after scores once you have deployed the files.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card p-5">
          <h3 class="font-semibold mb-2">How is this different from the free fix file generator?</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-gray-400">The free generator produces a generic skeleton from your homepage title and description. The Fix Pack is built by a human from your public pages, checked against your live robots.txt and schema, and verified with a re-audit after deployment. You are paying for the catalog work, the checking, and the verification — not for three files any chatbot can draft.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card p-5">
          <h3 class="font-semibold mb-2">Does llms.txt actually get read by AI engines?</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-gray-400">Rarely, on current evidence. Ahrefs' June 2026 study of 137,210 domains found 97% of published llms.txt files got zero requests in May 2026, and Google says it ignores the file. We include a hand-written llms.txt because it is free, harmless, and read by some agents and tools — but the measurable parts of this pack are the robots.txt access rules and the Product schema. We will never promise you citations.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card p-5">
          <h3 class="font-semibold mb-2">Do you guarantee rankings or AI citations?</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-gray-400">No — and no honest provider can. AI answers depend on the engines, your content, and your market. What we guarantee is the deliverable: correct, catalog-specific files, deployed-ready, plus a re-audit showing exactly what changed in your 11-dimension score.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card p-5">
          <h3 class="font-semibold mb-2">How do I order and pay?</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-gray-400">Email us your store URL at <a href="mailto:hello@geoscore.help" class="text-brand-400 hover:underline">hello@geoscore.help</a> first and get a free 1-paragraph diagnosis. If the diagnosis shows real gaps and you want to proceed, we complete and deliver the fix files within 48 hours, followed by a post-deployment re-audit.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card p-5">
          <h3 class="font-semibold mb-2">What do you need from me?</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-gray-400">Just your store URL and which product sells best. No admin access, no passwords. On Shopify, llms.txt is not a file you upload — the platform generates <span class="font-mono text-gray-300">/agents.md</span> and points <span class="font-mono text-gray-300">/llms.txt</span> at it, and the only supported override is a theme template. We write <span class="font-mono text-gray-300">templates/llms.txt.liquid</span> for you; your developer adds it in one step. We handle the two traps: a custom template <em>replaces</em> Shopify's output rather than merging with it, so it must carry the UCP and MCP discovery links across, and it renders in a restricted Liquid context where shop, collections and pages are blank — so the content is curated and static, and needs a refresh when your range changes.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <script is:inline type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify({
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'Service',
    name: 'AI Visibility Fix Pack',
    serviceType: 'GEO (Generative Engine Optimization) remediation',
    provider: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'GeoScore', url: 'https://geoscore.help' },
    description: 'Done-for-you GEO fix package: Product JSON-LD completed and validated for your best-seller, a robots.txt diagnosis, a curated llms.txt, a 1-page audit, and a post-deploy re-audit.',
    offers: { '@type': 'Offer', price: '49', priceCurrency: 'USD', name: 'AI Visibility Fix Pack (one-time)', availability: 'https://schema.org/InStock', url: 'https://geoscore.help/fixpack/' }
  })} />
</Layout>

<script>
  if (window.geoTrack) {
    window.geoTrack('fixpack_viewed', { source_type: window.geoSource ? window.geoSource() : 'other' });
  }
  var cta = document.getElementById('fixpack-email-cta');
  if (cta) {
    cta.addEventListener('click', function () {
      if (window.geoTrack) window.geoTrack('fixpack_cta_clicked', { placement: 'fixpack_page', transport_type: 'beacon' });
    });
  }
</script>
